{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Agent runtime: serving a Deployment on the user's machine",
  "description": "How the Janus Agent starts, keeps its Deployments across restarts, and serves each HTTP request by running the module.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus-agent/main.go",
      "line": 41,
      "title": "The Agent starts",
      "description": "`func main` is the Agent's entry point. It hands its arguments to run, which wires the runtime to the machine."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/cmd/janus-agent/main.go",
      "line": 50,
      "title": "Wiring the runtime",
      "description": "`func run` builds the runner, the local state and the host folder, then starts the runtime."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/agent_runtime.go",
      "line": 92,
      "title": "The runtime keeps its state locally",
      "description": "`func NewAgentRuntime` takes the runner and the LocalState port, so the Deployments and the pause survive a restart on this machine."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/agent_runtime.go",
      "line": 105,
      "title": "After a restart",
      "description": "`func (r *AgentRuntime) Start` loads the kept Deployments and serves them again, without a new Deploy. A module whose hash no longer matches is not served."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/agent_runtime.go",
      "line": 133,
      "title": "A Deploy is checked and probed",
      "description": "`func (r *AgentRuntime) Deploy` checks the module against its hash and runs one GET / probe. The Deployment is kept only if the probe ends cleanly."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/app/agent_runtime.go",
      "line": 273,
      "title": "Serving one request",
      "description": "`func (r *AgentRuntime) Serve` runs the module once for one request. Each request starts a fresh run."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/domain/cgi/cgi.go",
      "line": 43,
      "title": "The request goes in as CGI",
      "description": "`func Env` turns the request into the CGI environment the module reads. The body goes in on stdin."
    },
    {
      "file": "janus-go/internal/domain/cgi/cgi.go",
      "line": 93,
      "title": "The response comes out of stdout",
      "description": "`func ParseResponse` reads the module's output as the HTTP response. The status the module returns is passed through without judgement."
    }
  ]
}
